.	http://purl.oclc.org/NET/cmcs/schema/:hasConfigurations		<rdf:Bag xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" > <rdf:li><rdf:href xlink:href="Parameters/chemsys.mvm" xlink:type="simple"></rdf:href></rdf:li><rdf:li><rdf:href xlink:href="Parameters/BasisSet.ecce_basisset" xlink:type="simple"></rdf:href></rdf:li><rdf:li><rdf:href xlink:href="Parameters/SetupParams" xlink:type="simple"></rdf:href></rdf:li></rdf:Bag>
.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:annotation		ORCA, PBE0-D3BJ/def2-SVP with CPCM(water), optimisation, frequencies with IR and Raman. This calculation shows the S–O stretches of a sulfate bound through one oxygen in cis-[Co(en)2Cl(OSO3)], with the same Co(en)2 framework as the chelating and bridging complexes, so the sulfate bands can be compared directly. Chloride is the sixth ligand because it has no internal vibrations and its Co–Cl stretch lies near 300 cm⁻¹, below the sulfate and Co–O–S region.
.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:application		ORCA
